course: dictionary
lesson: 1807
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Clove is a good example: it can be a spice, a part of garlic, or an old past tense.
explain: «Add two cloves of garlic to the pan.» Garlic grows as a bulb, and a bulb is made of small pieces. Here cloves are the small pieces, not whole bulbs, so clove means one small section of garlic.
explain: «He clove the log in two.» There is no garlic and no spice here. He is doing something to the log, and it ends up in two parts. Clove is the old past tense of cleave, which means to split. Test it: he split the log in two. That fits, so that is the meaning.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a word with several meanings.
fact: A clove is a small, dried, nail-shaped flower bud used as a strong-smelling spice.
fact: Cloves come from a tree grown in Indonesia and Zanzibar, and they were very valuable in medieval Europe.
fact: Clove oil was used to numb toothache.
fact: «Cloves and nutmeg grew only on a few tiny islands in the Moluccas, now part of Indonesia.»
exercise: «Add two cloves of garlic to the pan.» What is a clove here? | A dried, nail-shaped flower bud used as a spice | A type of tree | *One small section of a bulb of garlic | The past tense of split
exercise: Nadia says «He clove the log in two» means he joined the log together. What does clove mean here? | Joined together | Burned to ash | *Split | Painted red
exercise: In «Cloves and nutmeg grew only on a few tiny islands», which meaning of clove fits? | A bird that lives on islands | A small section of garlic | *A dried, nail-shaped flower bud used as a spice | A sharp knife
test: «Mum put a clove in the mulled drink.» What does clove mean here? | *A dried, nail-shaped spice | The past tense of cleave | A kind of cake | A small section of garlic
test: Ella reads «He clove the rope with an axe» and asks what clove means. | Dropped on the ground | *Split in two | Tied tight | Washed clean
exam: In «Mix two cloves of garlic into the sauce», what do the words around clove tell you? | The word is in the past tense, so it means split | It means a flower, because sauce is made from flowers | Sauce is a kind of tree, so clove means a tree | *Garlic is nearby, so clove means a small section of garlic
